WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:07.834
Unsealed Southern District of New York documents map Canadian political infrastructure connections to the Epstein-Maxwell global trafficking network.

00:00:07.784 --> 00:00:14.454
Peter Nygard — a Canadian fashion mogul — operated a parallel trafficking operation from his Bahamas compound.

00:00:14.454 --> 00:00:19.875
The MC2 modeling agency connected to Jean-Luc Brunel provided a recruitment pipeline.

00:00:19.875 --> 00:00:23.659
The TerraMar Project functioned as a financial transit vehicle.

00:00:23.659 --> 00:00:26.727
The Canadian connections are not incidental.

00:00:26.727 --> 00:00:34.784
They represent documented intersections between political access, financial infrastructure, and the trafficking network's operational requirements.

00:00:34.784 --> 00:00:37.579
The SDNY files are public.

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:40.954
The Canadian political entanglement is verified.

00:00:40.954 --> 00:00:48.068
The question that remains is not whether the connections exist — it is why no Canadian law enforcement agency has acted on them.
